      "role": "user",
      "content": "i'm curious though, a lot of critics argue that even if Conrad was being critical of the \"system,\" the book itself is still fundamentally flawed because it uses the Africans as objects rather than people. do you think the book can still be considered a masterpiece of literature if it relies so heavily on these dehumanizing tropes to make its point?",
