      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Whether it's a masterpiece is a matter of subjective literary taste, but its artistic merit is often separated from its moral failings. The book is undeniably powerful in its exploration of psychological decay and the darkness of the human spirit. However, you can't ignore that its power is built upon a foundation of deeply flawed, racist representations of the colonized people. Some argue the literary brilliance excuses the prejudice, while others maintain the tropes make it fundamentally compromised art.",
      "source": "target",
